            "Stage 5, halt: haltreq gives allhalted and the core's debug_halted_o = 1.",
            "Stage 6, abstract commands and program buffer: x10 write and read round trip, a store and load to the data SRAM through the program buffer, dpc inside the firmware region and cmderr = 0.",
            "Stage 7, resume: allresumeack and allrunning, debug_running_o = 1, the core PC inside the firmware region and cmderr = 0.",
            "Stage 8, single step and trigger: dcsr.step advances exactly one instruction (new dpc, dcsr.cause = 4); an execute trigger on a loop address halts the core there with dcsr.cause = 2.",
            "Stage 9, ndmreset: the system resets while the debug module stays alive, the core halts at the reset vector (allhavereset, dpc = BOOT_ADDR, dcsr.cause = 3) and after resume the firmware prints its greeting a second time.",
            "Stage 10: DMI busy handling (op = 3, dtmcs.dmistat = 3, dmireset and dmihardreset) and accesses during an abstract command giving cmderr = 1, cleared by write-one-to-clear.",
            "Stages 11 and 12: exceptions in the program buffer give cmderr = 3 without corrupting dpc; unsupported abstract commands give cmderr = 2; a command while the core runs gives cmderr = 4.",
            "Stage 13: system bus access is tied off in the SoC, so sbcs reports sberror = 2, an unsupported size reports sberror = 4, the error clears and nothing hangs.",
            "Stage 14: discovery and WARL behaviour of the debug module registers (dmcontrol, hartinfo, abstractcs, haltsum, nextdm, progbuf0 to 8, data1, tinfo, tselect) and transfer with postexec.",
            "Stage 15: TAP behaviour, including IR capture 0b00101, BYPASS and undefined IR, Pause and Exit2 states, back-to-back scans without Idle, and recovery through Test-Logic-Reset and TRST in the middle of traffic.",
